{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nimport itertools\n\ndef invnum(seq):\n    N = len(seq)\n    res = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            if seq[i] > seq[j]:\n                res += 1\n    return res\n\ndef naive(N, k, flag):\n    res = 0\n    for p in itertools.permutations(range(N), N):\n        for q in itertools.permutations(range(N), N):\n            if ((p < q) or (not(flag))) and (invnum(p) - invnum(q) > k):\n                res += 1\n    return res\n\nn, mod = map(int, input().split())\n\n# Use lru_cache for memoization instead of manual dictionary\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\ndef solve(N, k, flag):\n    if N == 1:\n        res = -1\n        if flag:\n            res = 0\n        else:\n            if k < 0:\n                res = 1\n            else:\n                res = 0\n        return res\n    \n    invnum_INF = (N * (N - 1)) // 2\n    \n    if k < -invnum_INF - 1:\n        res = solve(N, -invnum_INF - 1, flag)\n        return res\n    \n    if k >= invnum_INF:\n        return 0\n    \n    res = 0\n    \n    for delta in range(-N + 1, N):\n        if flag and (delta > 0):\n            continue\n        wt = min(N - delta, delta + N)\n        res += solve(N - 1, k - delta, (delta == 0) & flag) * wt\n        res %= mod\n    \n    return res % mod\n\nans = solve(n, 0, 1) % mod\nprint(ans)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long invnum(const vector<int>& seq) {\n    int N = seq.size();\n    long long res = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < N; j++) {\n            if (seq[i] > seq[j]) {\n                res++;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nlong long naive(int N, long long k, bool flag) {\n    long long res = 0;\n    vector<int> perm(N);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) perm[i] = i;\n    \n    do {\n        vector<int> p = perm;\n        do {\n            vector<int> q = perm;\n            bool cond = false;\n            if (!flag) cond = true;\n            else if (p < q) cond = true;\n            \n            if (cond && (invnum(p) - invnum(q) > k)) {\n                res++;\n            }\n        } while (next_permutation(q.begin(), q.end()));\n    } while (next_permutation(p.begin(), p.end()));\n    \n    return res;\n}\n\nmap<tuple<int, long long, bool>, long long> memo;\n\nlong long solve(int N, long long k, bool flag) {\n    auto key = make_tuple(N, k, flag);\n    if (memo.find(key) != memo.end()) {\n        return memo[key];\n    }\n    \n    if (N == 1) {\n        long long res = -1;\n        if (flag) {\n            res = 0;\n        } else {\n            if (k < 0) {\n                res = 1;\n            } else {\n                res = 0;\n            }\n        }\n        memo[key] = res;\n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    long long invnum_INF = (long long)(N * (N - 1)) / 2;\n    \n    if (k < -invnum_INF - 1) {\n        long long res = solve(N, -invnum_INF - 1, flag);\n        memo[key] = res;\n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    if (k >= invnum_INF) {\n        memo[key] = 0;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    long long res = 0;\n    \n    for (int delta = -N + 1; delta < N; delta++) {\n        if (flag && (delta > 0)) {\n            continue;\n        }\n        long long wt = min(N - delta, delta + N);\n        res = (res + solve(N - 1, k - delta, (delta == 0) && flag) * wt) % mod;\n    }\n    \n    memo[key] = res % mod;\n    return res % mod;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, mod_val;\n    cin >> n >> mod_val;\n    \n    // Override global mod with mod_val\n    // Since mod is used in solve, we need to handle it differently\n    // We'll use a global variable for mod\n    static int mod = mod_val;\n    \n    // Reset memoization\n    memo.clear();\n    \n    long long ans = solve(n, 0, true) % mod_val;\n    cout << ans << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.35\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.16677454370074e-05, -7.510157047363464e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.0397906812140718e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.006520661525428295, -7.152555099310121e-07, -7.986990567587782e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.013736126013100147, -9.536738616588991e-07, -4.172316494077677e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.25104066729545593, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.4676019165781327e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.15398213267326355, -1.9073304429184645e-05, -0.003178665181621909, -4.410734163684538e-06, -0.18180996179580688, -0.026300910860300064, -0.6931931972503662, -5.006777428206988e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -0.16332177817821503, -1.1801649634435307e-05, -0.320863276720047, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.04790939763188362, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -8.487341256113723e-05, -3.564294092939235e-05, -7.629365427419543e-06, -5.722029527532868e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0003805628512054682, -5.9